WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.860
Let’s look at the shoulders, and how they help you reach.

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:09.470
PsA can affect a shoulder joint, and the tissues around it.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.180
The shoulder can become inflamed and painful.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:18.590
Pain may make it hard to reach up, or to put on a shirt.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:26.600
Joints may feel stiff, and stiffness is often worse in the morning, or after resting.

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:31.490
A sore shoulder can have more than one cause.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:36.040
The body map shows a place to discuss, not a diagnosis.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:41.450
Tell your team which shoulder hurts, and when the pain began.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.810
Describe a task that has become harder, such as reaching a shelf.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:51.060
Mention stiffness, swelling, or a change in how far you can move.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:56.190
Your team can check the joint, and the tissues around it.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:01:00.240
A physical therapist can help improve how a joint works.

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:04.310
Great job! Let’s review.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.000
A sore shoulder can have more than one cause.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:12.360
Describe a task that has become harder, such as reaching a shelf.
